            "size": "52px",
            "weight": 600
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "subtitle",
          "type": "text",
          "enabled": true,
          "order": 2,
          "props": {
            "text": "I'm Theo Yamada, Associate Professor in the School of Computer Science at Carnegie Mellon. My lab studies the gap between ML research and ML engineering — specifically, why so much rigorous work never makes it into a single production system. We publish papers in NeurIPS and ICLR, but every paper ships with a reference implementation that runs on a single GPU and a tutorial-grade README. If a senior engineer can't reproduce our results in a weekend, we consider the paper unfinished."
          }
        },
        {
